WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.682 --> 00:00:04.582
Eh, quick one. It rains, and you carry umbrella.

2
00:00:04.602 --> 00:00:05.692
You get WET or not?

3
00:00:07.182 --> 00:00:09.329
Logic cannot answer by feeling one.

4
00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:12.182
It needs a formula, and it needs to know which letters

5
00:00:12.202 --> 00:00:13.132
are true.

6
00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.359
So today, 4 things lah.

7
00:00:15.379 --> 00:00:20.546
First, the 3 parts of a logic: syntax, semantics, calculus.

8
00:00:20.566 --> 00:00:24.266
Second, how to build a truth table without kena the famous

9
00:00:24.286 --> 00:00:28.986
arrow trap. Third, what is a MODEL, and the words satisfiable,

10
00:00:29.006 --> 00:00:34.666
valid, unsatisfiable. Last one, entailment: when does a knowledge base force

11
00:00:34.686 --> 00:00:36.386
a sentence to be true?

12
00:00:36.406 --> 00:00:39.016
All pen and paper, same like the exam.

13
00:00:41.001 --> 00:00:42.501
The 3 parts ah.

14
00:00:42.521 --> 00:00:46.261
SYNTAX is spelling: this string, legal formula or not?

15
00:00:46.281 --> 00:00:48.821
P arrow not Q, legal.

16
00:00:48.841 --> 00:00:51.451
P arrow and Q, rubbish.

17
00:00:51.481 --> 00:00:55.701
SEMANTICS is meaning: give every letter true or false, then the

18
00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:58.251
formula also become true or false.

19
00:00:58.281 --> 00:01:01.221
CALCULUS is the procedure to work it out, like a truth

20
00:01:01.241 --> 00:01:02.011
table.

21
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:03.861
Now the 5 connectives.

22
00:01:03.881 --> 00:01:06.581
Not, and, or: easy lah.

23
00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:10.741
But the arrow, if P then Q, this one tricky.

24
00:01:10.761 --> 00:01:14.901
It is false in only 1 row: P true, Q false.

25
00:01:14.921 --> 00:01:18.661
A promise, broken. When P is false, where got promise to

26
00:01:18.681 --> 00:01:21.421
break? So the arrow is TRUE.

27
00:01:21.441 --> 00:01:23.421
False arrow true: true.

28
00:01:23.441 --> 00:01:25.901
False arrow false: also true!

29
00:01:25.921 --> 00:01:28.851
Alamak, most wrong cells come from here.

30
00:01:29.225 --> 00:01:33.461
And the double arrow, P if and only if Q: true

31
00:01:33.481 --> 00:01:35.101
when both sides SAME.

32
00:01:35.121 --> 00:01:36.851
Both false also count hor.

33
00:01:38.867 --> 00:01:40.997
Okay, build one table.

34
00:01:41.027 --> 00:01:45.327
P: it rains. Q: you carry umbrella.

35
00:01:45.347 --> 00:01:47.247
R: you get wet.

36
00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:52.127
The sentence: rain makes you wet, AND umbrella keeps you dry.

37
00:01:52.147 --> 00:01:57.007
In symbols: if P then R, and, if Q then not

38
00:01:57.027 --> 00:01:57.917
R.

39
00:01:58.046 --> 00:02:02.207
Step 1: 3 letters, so 2 times 2 times 2, 8

40
00:02:02.227 --> 00:02:06.607
rows. Start with T T T, end with F F F,

41
00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:09.087
the right letter flip fastest.

42
00:02:09.107 --> 00:02:11.287
Step 2: helper columns.

43
00:02:11.307 --> 00:02:14.447
Not R. Then if P then R.

44
00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:17.007
Then if Q then not R.

45
00:02:17.027 --> 00:02:21.807
Step 3: the whole formula LAST, just and the 2 helper

46
00:02:21.827 --> 00:02:23.237
columns together.

47
00:02:23.484 --> 00:02:26.237
Look at row 3: T, F, T.

48
00:02:26.387 --> 00:02:28.637
Rain, no umbrella, wet.

49
00:02:28.707 --> 00:02:30.797
Both rules happy, so T.

50
00:02:30.949 --> 00:02:35.009
Now count the T in the last column: rows 3, 6,

51
00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:36.079
7 and 8.

52
00:02:36.229 --> 00:02:39.409
A MODEL is just a row that makes the formula true,

53
00:02:39.429 --> 00:02:42.319
so 4 models. Got at least 1 model?

54
00:02:42.389 --> 00:02:43.599
Satisfiable.

55
00:02:43.749 --> 00:02:45.169
All 8 rows T?

56
00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:45.999
Valid.

57
00:02:46.069 --> 00:02:46.719
Zero?

58
00:02:46.789 --> 00:02:48.159
Unsatisfiable.

59
00:02:48.309 --> 00:02:51.679
Ours: satisfiable, but not valid lor.

60
00:02:53.743 --> 00:02:58.123
Last idea, entailment. Put the 2 rules in a knowledge base,

61
00:02:58.143 --> 00:03:01.393
KB. Its models are the same 4 rows.

62
00:03:01.423 --> 00:03:06.043
KB entails alpha means: alpha is true in EVERY model of

63
00:03:06.063 --> 00:03:10.113
KB. So cover the other rows, look at those 4 only.

64
00:03:10.147 --> 00:03:13.007
Try this one: not, P and Q.

65
00:03:13.027 --> 00:03:17.167
In rows 3, 6, 7 and 8, P and Q never

66
00:03:17.187 --> 00:03:19.887
both true. So yes, entailed!

67
00:03:19.907 --> 00:03:24.167
The 2 rules secretly say rain and umbrella never come together.

68
00:03:24.187 --> 00:03:26.517
Wah, logic very strict sia.

69
00:03:26.553 --> 00:03:30.213
Now try R. Row 6 is a model, but R is

70
00:03:30.233 --> 00:03:34.297
false there. 1 counter-row is enough: NOT entailed.

71
00:03:34.317 --> 00:03:38.617
So remember: the arrow is false only for true then false,

72
00:03:38.637 --> 00:03:41.897
and entailed means true in ALL the models.

73
00:03:41.917 --> 00:03:46.497
The practice notebook got 6 exercises: truth tables with gaps, model

74
00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:50.537
or not, entailment by table, plus a small table printer to

75
00:03:50.557 --> 00:03:51.777
check your hand work.

76
00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:54.857
Graded work must be your own hor, the course does not

77
00:03:54.877 --> 00:03:56.887
allow AI there. Jia you!
